			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1940,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d5c3663dbab93cea",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Borrowed Cognition",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1780,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e3183dd9b09473e2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Applied Philosophy\n(why care what old farts said?)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":2020,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d022ab948cad31e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Story",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1160,
			"y":-2040,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a31125fe7f361270",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Religion without Faith",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":2100,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"957290679387b8f7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1. note transfer\n2. note transfer / brief font exp",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2060,
			"y":1580,
			"width":480,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"fe86ab82480ab065",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Act I",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1740,
			"y":560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9072b482a13764b5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"- Rent transport vans, tetris furniture\n- Multiple vans per day possible\n- If you get a driver -> iwabo (they know location)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1700,
			"y":640,
			"width":260,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"7e50a73aa905894f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"14.09.2024",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":520,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4208d0d3f574f5bf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"26.06.2026",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"54f7274267834571",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"cat approach:\ndont preach, instead\nBut wants to send a message\n\nHere’s me sharing what I think is beautiful",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1920,
			"y":240,
			"width":260,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"6f4f160bdc77818c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"When a system reaches a certain complexity it becomes nigh unpredictable both in what it does and in how it’s understood.\n\nBut There is a quality in that. But to try and control it..?\n\nYou can intentionally let go. Is what happened after intentional?\n\nWhen did you become so pensive?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1640,
			"y":-120,
			"width":260,
			"height":380
		},
		{
			"id":"5bf9b4fa24faeb52",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Add full books/texts of public domain works (+export func)(+april/mary-ann annotations)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1640,
			"y":280,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"07b591c37afb8183",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The only character allowed to make erratic decisions is the player. Everyone else must be smart people doing smart things. Even if the player isn’t.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1920,
			"y":-80,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"c53473d89735cedc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Tassen fallen, keine Tassen!",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1920,
			"y":80,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"cf85202b2046c499",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Artist is something others should call you",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1920,
			"y":160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"41c5a717d3e43f63",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Want to do good but can’t. Makes someone else, someone stronger do it for them. Is it their good that’s been done?\n\nI’ve created good where there was none.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":400,
			"width":260,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"dc87991df32a396f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Certainty at a cost",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":640,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"47d8404a0b853a8a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Iwabo is a game about control. And fear. The balance between acceptance and defiance. Family. Conservation.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":720,
			"width":260,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"6e89f2a5bf8c3e73",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Themes / Questions / Philosophy",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-820,
			"y":320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4ebaee4e4165a938",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What point is served by telling someone they have to apologise?\n\n  \n\nMany of the character driven story beats depend on Daryl’s input. But even the best advice wouldn’t be as essential in shaping them into “good” people, if they had any outside influence whatsoever.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":480,
			"width":260,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"9f8b28e6eae10159",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**building a foundation before you know any better. And the disproportionate value we as a society attribute to sticking to it.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":540,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"e7a7183d5b297ca4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Heidegger and dwelling**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":700,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4aa76be0a4ea6aa6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Nudity and the Church**\nCount Sternberg",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":780,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8a8aabf36f9db1e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Go full religion:\nDaryl turns to god and eventually is heard! The player for the first time doesn’t speak for Daryl, but to him!\n\nThis can imply two things: \n1 - you are the god who’s watching. The god outside the machine.\n2 - Or you are still Daryl, but disassociating from the self, to play your own god.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-420,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"6c22ef6813709ec7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"UX",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-760,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5ba6abf78db8713c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Weighted Dice - can manipulate all throws in your favour or against.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1060,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"b66c391b24d71af6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Unlucky - things don’t often go your way. But failure suits you, charming in its of way.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1060,
			"y":-300,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"926a55c9e3b185bd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Allergies - can’t eat everything, but hyper aware of ingredients, nutri stats etc",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1060,
			"y":-180,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"a9da0b285eaeb86b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Art-Critic",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1060,
			"y":-60,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"abcabc61c3afc523",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Sales man + art afficionado = art dealer",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1060,
			"y":20,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f7e09100ff0c1b31",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Mechanics",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1380,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6cd83b9d0d1969e0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Walls closing in, letterboxing, the lower the mood",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"30f7b4758debd41e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The main menu is a fridge with child drawings etc?\nThe fridge represents the need to conserve and coldness it takes to do what’s necessary. The family is put front and center yet feels tacked on and somewhat shallow. The food inside, over time, turns.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-340,
			"width":260,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"f8237c74da98e94b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Use marble sculpture?\n\nReligious connotation\nMisconception and idealization of a past that never was",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-80,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"7cab449332d44b05",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Go even further?\nif something major happens:\nThe father realises, the marble cracks!",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":80,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"532e754fe74b50d0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The way you see the world might change. Same world, different skin. Depending on your choices and worldview this skin could be altered or exchanged.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1420,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"606cd7d33e4f320b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Drugs and alcohol as a crutch when the going gets tough.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ba7ba863c01221d0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Hanging Paintings:\n\nDecoration slots. Discover them by looking around or buying them.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":-340,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"2f49a30ea2737c93",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The player can learn much earlier that the world probably didn’t end, at which point it’s their character they need to build to make him admit it to himself and his family.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1420,
			"y":-220,
			"width":260,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"3625931f07c9157c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Maybe resource management doesn’t need to be that big a factor? Look at how Twd s1 handled it. Many small actions have an impact on how characters see Lee. Might this be enough?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":-180,
			"width":260,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"41bf43e31734dff0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Clear mechanics to manipulate \n\nBoth into going to the bunker, but also leaving it.\n\nThe second one is pointed out that Daryl still thinks he’s the he arbiter of what should be done. That his skill gives him the right to decide for others.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1420,
			"y":-20,
			"width":260,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"bc992fd41817927d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Emoengine\n\nCharacter expressions should remain consistent between dialogue blocks. Blocks can alter or add nuance. Certain emotional states don’t allow for certain dialogue. Test this!!",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":40,
			"width":260,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"289d32be10014a7a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Daryl comes up with stories and fables and myths to explain things or to motivate the kids to do their chores",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":280,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"7a4eb9c0d463312c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Bonuses on skill checks for acting appropriately\n\n-> dominance? -> stand on above them, orate down\n\nIncentivize through interesting camera angles",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1420,
			"y":300,
			"width":260,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"12d3e577729b72b9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"April has a wall full of plants cascading down. However, keeping them alive requires constant power.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":420,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"d5fbfe9f1d6a5a6c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Add eLiza to the game, for Daryl to talk to?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1420,
			"y":540,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8662a864d6608b89",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Choices",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2220,
			"y":-1560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"756a73bdb5ee6c68",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Give money to charity?\nHelp out brother?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2280,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"743ebbb9c2b7f01e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Everything bad happens at once\n\nWar breaks out\nDomestic terrorism\nStreet fights\nPandemic\nNuclear war threat\nNuclear testing\nDoomsday prognosis\nNatural disaster",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1480,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"d5eb7fc73df1e968",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"I WON’T END LIKE HER\n\nWhat does the end of the world mean to an artist who spent her life creating for social recognition?\u0003\n\nSkilled artist with nothing to say.\n\n-April",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2040,
			"y":-1960,
			"width":260,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"469f125057d11bb9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Characters have favourite meals",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1420,
			"y":620,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ac8591b6e8e5d92e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Not keeping track of calendar makes it difficult to remember birthdays",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":640,
			"width":260,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"e40d77138b8ca439",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Can you train them to do your bidding? (Reward/punishment)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":740,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9f02cfd04a74b260",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Remember / Forget Birthdays etc",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2d77445876732e82",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Backstory",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1160,
			"y":-1560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"47c0c5e6ad288dd2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Harold, while straight, used moneybags’ being gay to his advantage. He gave up some part of his masculinity to save his son.\n\nWhy did he die in a care facility?\n\nWhere are your siblings? \n\nWhy only us?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"66baae61e0a2e7b2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The only truly bad ending is the characters not addressing any of the issues between them but sticking together out of a feeling of obligation, being miserable.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1960,
			"width":260,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"68922570cf4354a6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"BEING YOURSELF IS DANGEROUS\n\nHow do you choose between who people need you to be with who you are. Especially if you don’t seem to be good at being yourself?\u0003\n\nGifted mechanic, terrible artist. Trans - but can’t express it - yet.\n\n-June",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2320,
			"y":-1960,
			"width":260,
			"height":340
		},
		{
			"id":"375afc4be3c45b52",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"FAMILY MATTERS MOST  \n\nWhat if, in trying to save your family, you are the one who hurt them most?\u0003\u0003  \nLoving dad who would do anything to protect his tribe, except question what that means.  \n\n-Daryl",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1480,
			"y":-1960,
			"width":260,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"9666f2eb39f89177",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"POTENTIAL ISN’T ENOUGH \n\nHow do you love a child you blame for the life you never wanted-pushed to live your dream, and resented for succeeding?  \n\nChild prodigy turned housewife.  \n\n-Mary-Ann",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1760,
			"y":-1960,
			"width":260,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"a0feed149ec2f74b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Events",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1160,
			"y":-1560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"38957ccd05ffcd21",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Hunting ghosts (?)\nNo matter how many books, always more outside\n\nContinuations\n\nEmergency",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"1584922057b37837",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Playing hide and seek kid goes where they shouldn’t",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c35d16af55d4b6b6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Playing hide and seek; kid “too old”",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1400,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"649821d928f6ef1c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Tree roots growing through ceiling",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c807c990547bebd8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Accidents, sickness, someone chokes on food",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1240,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9a651d3a97ffaebc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Runs out of Paint (starts using rations)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1240,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b1002a74d430f23a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Runs out of paper (starts painting on walls)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3577b29cdaac3450",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Kids talk about what they would have been, had things been different.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"5da253915011c183",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Already at the bunker?\n\nWatch the sun go down before locking yourself in.\n\nBirds flying low.\n\n  \n\nWaiting for the end? Sundown.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1360,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"533b340871aac769",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Rushing to the bunker. Heavy storm to dead of night.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d2734bc25e601a19",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"April does the dust blow cave painting, using June as the model\n\nNaturally June is covered head to toe in dust\nYou find her, June laughing April looking ertappt\nHuge mess\n\nArt critic\n-> will notice the implication\nDo you commend the work?\nDo you shut it down?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"e44cd969a488dac2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Why not sell the bunker?\n\nA lot of the games weight (actually not a lot, or at least not most, seeing that they will never get the years they lost back), hinges on them coming out of it with nothing, having left their house and everything behind. There are a few ways to attempt to fix this.\n\n  \n\n1 - when the attempt to sell it, the government or relatives of moneybags seize the property.\n\n  \n\n2 - selling it causes the cycle to continue. the only bidder is clearly planning to move his family there. And the characters decide against it because they dont want them to experience the same they do.\n\n  \n\n3 - they seal the bunker when they leave it\n\n  \n\n4 - they move back into the bunker, only coming out occasionally",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":0,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":540,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"dcc7933c60744547",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Kids find /play with /hurt with gun",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":560,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"96cbf7201f5e4bfa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Environment",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1160,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5e9ef47ae898ce46",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Silo the only place for a tree\nOr a trash heap",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1100,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"0ad6ce3690133914",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"How would even god know to find me?\n\nMany Aprils buried.\n\nUnderground\n\n  \n\nMakes me wish for\n\nNo more gilded Cage\n\nTurned to stone\n\n  \n\nGrave mistake\n\nNo Achieving heaven unless buried",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1640,
			"y":-620,
			"width":260,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"42a156dbe163a309",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"only way to heaven is undergroud",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1640,
			"y":-200,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"67ac1e34c17e5e1b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**The storm is a day early**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"058433a186414683",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Go full religion. Play baroque music preach from the pulpit that is the service stair to the second floor.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1020,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"49fa71902537efd9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"He takes April hunting again, she needs to learn\n\nI don’t want to kill it\n\nYou cant afford to be that person if you want to survive with us.\n\nAnd you not surviving with us is not an option.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-880,
			"width":260,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"7448ba66724fffc5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Much like Daryl spending loads of food and time on gym maxing, eventually the player notices Mary-Ann “letting herself go”. The player can accept or respect this, but also call it out. Which may lead to her becoming much less effective at everything else. Time and effort spent on looking good, that could be spent on maintenance and frankly - rest.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-940,
			"width":260,
			"height":340
		},
		{
			"id":"253f0f60fbde00b9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"June disassembles something",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-620,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"46b9fc42fd967549",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**You’re not going to win any awards with that one**\n\nOkay? Who cares?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1080,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"c834f24f09d65a50",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"June tries to carry a heavy food bucket and drops it. Do you try and scrape it back in? Accept the loss, scold her?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1160,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"e8885cff8befa1b7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Masturbatory\n\nWhat’s wrong with masturbation? As long as I don’t expect people to ooh and aah at my brilliance. Besides, plenty of women have made good bank with that sort of thing in their bedrooms, so why shouldn’t in my study?\n\nWait, what do you know about women in bedrooms?\n\nWe did have the internet didn’t we?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":0,
			"y":-1060,
			"width":260,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"f7f09810e99753cb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Telling June Santa isnt real",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-900,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"533c92469780b7f5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"June loses a Tooth",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-820,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"723e287c0c2b287e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"They fight over their interpretations of a book. But not over what’s right or wrong, but rather over who gets the book",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1080,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"9e808b2dada093e2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Someone falls into the rising water in the silo\n\nThey swim in standing water",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-920,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"4afd5ea919af9eb6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"april and june play catch and knock over the food table",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-780,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"45623c6d89d9d0c8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"mary-ann breaks apils guitar",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-700,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"96df3bb6fefac1d3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**April snaps out of it by telling off Maryann for letting herself go and Mary Ann retorting she’s doing the same thing. But she does so out of a feeing of superiority, and must later uplift ma as well to redeem this.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-1100,
			"width":260,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"d8071d760c1bb7cf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**April goes on a journey to discover other religions**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-860,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"515aed9087b74054",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"[Perspective Paintings, Religion](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/EN0PHj0P__M)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":400,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"89397f60e4408000",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"References",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":160,
			"y":340,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a5d047ea6d936a61",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Dumbbells\nYou’re strong and fit and the other things. True alpha.\n\nMaintaining your mass means eating more, spending time exercising and costly equipment. \n\nCan’t pay too much for beauty.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":20,
			"width":260,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"b886e9c40f1dbeb6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Misc",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1960,
			"y":-720,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c499424705d4ca1d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Apocalypse did happen.\n\nPeople turn up with things to trade.\n\nShoot them immediately?\n\nSets off sequence of events where the mostly peaceful group grows resentful towards Daryl and decides to steer clear. No trade, no exchange. Further isolation. Eventually a well armed group turns up. They, too wish to trade.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1920,
			"y":-620,
			"width":260,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"2d6fcfd594dcc94c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Everyone distrustful, selfish and rich/powerful enough to hide in bunkers and facilities left the world to those who weren’t. A utopia is born.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1920,
			"y":-240,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"0a0e12ce48d643c0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Mary-Ann finds her faith once more or never finds god again but finds comfort in ritual",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-740,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"a14f0d67f73461cf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Forgot Junes Birthday",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-1060,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"579440b55f9108fb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"(Forgot) Wedding Anniversary",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-980,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"92603f04b85dcdaf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Mary-Ann isn’t too happy with June reading about other religions. To her they’re more curiosities rather than “serious religion”",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-780,
			"width":260,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"f2bf35a697037258",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"- Assumed authority\n- Consequent responsibility \n- Fear and Failure\n- Family",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":400,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"784d8b017920038a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Btb Josh Duggar",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b4513b8fa529cc9c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Culture “war”\n\nQuiverful by [Kathryn Joyce](https://www.amazon.de/-/en/Kathryn-Joyce/e/B001JSBTGG/ref=dp_byline_cont_book_1)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":500,
			"width":260,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"a385a299b8f8f8d5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Morale",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fcff41e5e11fa2e9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Rim world mood buffs, adding up, trigger rolls.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-80,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"eef49cfa59ec1f0c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Traits",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":240,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"724fa120ebc5d20b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Make skill checks easier or harder by setting “goal “ with better or worse rewards.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"e99e7492460264a9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Consider the groups that would wind up in the bunker, the traits between them, overlaps, differences, use that as basis for the skills/items",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-300,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"78515ed3d9826e25",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Skills:\nIntrusive thoughts",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-140,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5aa92fc7a84c37e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Dice - Gambler, +1 on all checks, can see the odds?**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-60,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fa2adbb00d164a6f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Bill Gothard\nInstitute to basic life principles",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"495ade149062d288",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Carver clementine dialogue boss battle twd s 2**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":680,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0a7b2a05af7e18f3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Quirks",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1000,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"61be34423156b3f6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paranoia - Foresight +\n\nActing in character rewarded different from against character (growth)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":560,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"85c61ebaf62e6f67",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Schopenhauer",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":760,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"89dee6aa8e70af46",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"It is an examination of Pascal’s wager through the lens of the ethics of care.\n\nRelational Ethics?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":800,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"689207a614f627e7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Shooting range, gun safety (leaving gun lying around)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1700,
			"y":820,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2729e36c5f914380",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"B route in act 1 is seeking therapy\n\nSo essentially:  \nI want to sell the player on the impending apocalypse. Easiest way to, regardless of actual “cause” is to create a meta narrative reinforcing that belief. B route end is waking up at the beginning after facing the uncertainty, mirroring a game over screen. Time limit during the day suggests urgency to act (and could be complete bullshit). The further you fall behind on prepping, the more it seems to be on the news. A heartbeat sound somewhere in the far distance. The screen tinting to a shade of red over time. Things like that.\n\nYou alleviate these symptoms by working towards the bunker.\n\nOr, by seeking therapy.\n\nIn that case the secret end ends the world actually. Haha",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1700,
			"y":860,
			"width":260,
			"height":760
		},
		{
			"id":"e8f765f8f5ecbcd1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Leviathanism\nalmighty force presiding over peace",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":860,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"60b7eaaaf717411f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"18.04.2025 -> checkout",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1320,
			"y":840,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2336e6d11253b363",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The second Sex",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":840,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"25affef9d667c2b8",
